 4. 🏀 Double dribble 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The NBA's ownership merry-go-round is spinning furiously, Axios' Dan Primack writes .

 The latest: Marc Lore has agreed to sell his control stake in the NBA's Minnesota Timberwolves and the WNBA's Minnesota Lynx to billionaire investor Marc Stad at a $4.5 billion enterprise value, Axios has confirmed. It comes just a week after Mark Walter agreed to sell the Los Angeles Lakers to Joshua Kushner and Bob Iger for $12.5 billion. Zoom in: Lore, a serial entrepreneur ( Diapers.com , Wonder ) and former Walmart exec, gained control of the T-Wolves just last summer, after a protracted legal process .

 Lore's partner on the deal, ex-MLB player Alex Rodriguez, will remain as part of club ownership. Stad was a limited partner but now takes a more prominent role. Lore is likely to retain a small position. Go deeper 

 
 
